Follow-up to k112. Per ADR 0001 (rule 2 + 5) new fields are added additively, and only once something needs them. maint/spec-overlay.yaml is the mechanism (k112, 84506ef). The 8 NEW FIELDs of `perl maint/spec-drift-check.pl --from spec/v1.51.yaml --to spec/v1.55.yaml`:

- ContainerSummary.Health -- the most useful one: container health in `containers->list` without an inspect per container
- ContainerInspectResponse.Storage
- ContainerStatsResponse.os_type
- SystemInfo.NRI
- TaskSpec::Resources.MemorySwappiness, .SwapBytes
- ImageInspect.Identity, ImageManifestSummary::ImageData.Identity -- stay OUT: they pull in the signature/attestation cluster (decided on k112, recorded in maint/spec-overlay.yaml)

Each graft: an overlay entry, the new nested classes it needs, a fixture captured from a live engine (name engine + version), and a Changes entry. Until then every one of these is reachable in unknown_fields (measured k110). Lane: api-docker-type-writer.
